{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — PAGE FAQ SCHEMA (2026-08-03)
  Rendered from lbass-entity-schema.liquid, which is in <head> on every
  template (including the homepage, which uses {% layout none %} and so never
  sees layout/theme.liquid).

  WHY IT IS GATED SO TIGHTLY
  templates/page.liquid hardcodes FAQPage markup for a few specific handles.
  Any NEW page — /pages/faq included — gets none, which is why that page
  shipped with 12 visible questions and 0 in schema.

  This emits FAQPage ONLY when the page carries a lbass.faq metafield. No
  metafield, no markup. FAQPage without matching visible Q&A is a
  structured-data violation, so the gate is the point — it must never fire
  speculatively.

  DRIFT WARNING
  The visible Q&A lives in the page BODY; the schema is built from the
  METAFIELD. Two copies, nothing enforcing agreement. Edit one, edit the other.
  (templates/article.liquid does not have this problem — there the metafield is
  the single source for both the visible list and the schema.)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign pg_faq = page.metafields.lbass.faq.value -%}
{%- if pg_faq != blank -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "@id": "{{ shop.url }}{{ page.url }}#faq",
  "inLanguage": "ar-MA",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for item in pg_faq -%}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ item.q | json }},
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | json }} }
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
